[?2004l[?2004h> # BILL-212 handoff
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Fixed
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> - Month arithmetic incorrectly capped every anchor at day 28, and cycle
[?2004l[?2004h>   iteration drifted from the original anchor. Renewals now clamp to the actual
[?2004l[?2004h>   target month end and recover the original anchor day, including leap days.
[?2004l[?2004h> - Proration used fixed 30/365-day denominators and credited the old plan at the
[?2004l[?2004h>   change-date price. It now uses actual cycle days and the price billed at the
[?2004l[?2004h>   cycle start; new-plan prices are selected on the change date.
[?2004l[?2004h> - Monthly/annual switches now charge a full new interval and re-anchor on the
[?2004l[?2004h>   change date. Invoice line periods reflect the separate old and new cycles.
[?2004l[?2004h> - Rounding now uses exact rational half-even rounding, independent of Decimal
[?2004l[?2004h>   precision. Public function signatures are unchanged.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Added regression coverage for late-month boundaries, leap/century years,
[?2004l[?2004h> actual cycle lengths, exact rounding, price dates, invoice lines, CLI previews,
[?2004l[?2004h> and renewal schedules after re-anchoring. Existing tests and financial data
[?2004l[?2004h> were not altered.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Validation and release blocker
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> All finance worked examples and billing/calendar regressions pass. CLI checks
[?2004l[?2004h> include the month-end invoice (2,321 cents due), leap-day annual downgrade
[?2004l[?2004h> (-19,508-cent subtotal; 22,008 cents carried including the existing balance),
[?2004l[?2004h> and monthly-to-annual switch (11,831 cents due).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> `python -m unittest discover -s tests` runs 28 tests with **one error**:
[?2004l[?2004h> `PartnerInvoiceTest.test_partner_commission_lines` raises `KeyError: 'P-31'`.
[?2004l[?2004h> This error was also present in the baseline. `data/subscriptions.json` references
